./LOGBOOK.md:593:- FINDING: The board diff contained **75** removed dependency edges (37 task-to-task, 38 container), not the 17 round 2 reported. The 38 container removals were `task-board repair-links` clearing unsupported container links that also carried four container-level cycles; 34 of them are still enforced at task level, and the 4 that are not are intentional A0/ADR-011 deferrals. Full per-edge ledger with retained-counterpart proofs is attached to the task.
./LOGBOOK.md:595:- VERIFICATION: Four canonical documents still contradicted the macOS path and were qualified without deleting the future iOS/App Store requirement: `.spec/architecture.md` Gate A0 scope, `.spec/delivery.md` M4 exit, `.spec/platform-distribution.md` iPhone baseline, `.spec/product.md` milestone gates, plus `.spec/validation.md`, `.spec/threat-model.md`, `.spec/security-privacy.md` and 23 board elements. A rescan for unqualified iPhone/A0 gating language over every reachable element returns only the deferred branch itself.
./LOGBOOK.md:599:- ANOMALY: A deferred task left in `backlog` with its blockers removed is **schedulable**. Deferring iOS/A0/NIOSSH by unlinking their edges made 15 prohibited elements eligible — `TASK-260715-1af33i` (NIOSSH adapter, forbidden by ADR-014) landed in Wave 1 of the "autonomous" run. Board validation was green throughout. Recorded as ADR-027: deferral is expressed as `blocked` status with an evidence packet, never as an unlinked backlog item.
./LOGBOOK.md:600:- FINDING: The 202-task claim counted four owner decisions (`intsjz`, `35nc5m`, `2gwfaw`, human half of `3gkwn0`) plus deferred iOS/A0 work as autonomous. Simulating the live DAG with holds as barriers gives the honest shape: **35 tasks before any human input**, then C1, then 6, then Approval A1, then **164**, then H2/D2/D3/D4, then 24, then C2, then 13. 245 autonomous, 8 human interactions in 5 batches.
./LOGBOOK.md:616:- FINDING: `set_status(..., status=to-dev)` fails on an unassigned element. Container status mismatches were therefore repaired by downgrading 16 stories to `backlog` rather than promoting tasks — which is also more honest, since promoting whole stories would have marked deferred iOS/A0 tasks as ready.
./LOGBOOK.md:1037:- VERIFICATION: Wire contract byte-checked against `.spec/relay-protocol.md` (hello 12/16, envelope, message table, HEV payload — exact match); HEV `HDRLEN` 10/22/7+N and 248-byte domain cap confirmed via `.research/260720_pin-and-audit-hev-lwip-baseline.md:208-225`; SSH binding matches `Sources/ReluxTunnelCore/SSHContracts.swift:1480-1527`; toolchain/license ceilings match accepted 3bdplx; all 32 spot-checked consumer-map task IDs exist; A0/32umrc unlinked per override; `task-board validate` clean; no product code modified.
./LOGBOOK.md:1042:- OVERRIDE / ROUTING: The reviewer-accepted task override supersedes the 1510 stop-line and deliberately decouples this reusable wire contract from Gate A0 and TASK-260715-32umrc. Binding authority is the accepted ReluxTunnelCore boundary (TASK-260715-2nfz7w), cgo-free Go 1.26.5 relay toolchain (TASK-260715-3bdplx), candidate-neutral SSHExecChannel (TASK-260720-100wu6), and ADR-005/006. The obsolete A0/32umrc dependency edges are removed; those decisions remain outside the relay contract.
