+# TASK-260715-whtdsf — Rework 4 outcome
+
+Date: 2026-08-30 (Asia/Tbilisi)
+Base: `b3422b05226253a17676b9b84c764071fe3dbe74`
+
+## Result
+
+Ready for exact-artifact independent agent review. The CI trust and
+quality-gate contract now closes CR revision 2's release workflow-provenance
+blocker while preserving every prior accepted control.
+
+- A `v*` tag triggers only unprivileged `release-intake.yml`. Repository
+  settings enforce a read-only token, production secrets exist only in
+  protected environments restricted to the default branch, and intake exposes
+  no cache, artifact, checkout, executable output, or candidate authority.
+- Candidate acceptance occurs only in default-branch `release-prepare.yml` via
+  `workflow_run: completed`. It independently resolves run/ref/ancestry
+  metadata and rejects missing or ambiguous evidence without consuming intake
+  code, output, cache, artifact, log, or asserted verdict.
+- `github.workflow_sha`, a checked-in policy digest, and every
+  credential-capable reusable workflow's full commit SHA/file digest are bound
+  into the immutable candidate. Relative, tag, branch, candidate-ref, and
+  selectable-ref release authority is prohibited.
+- Production-call-site negative fixtures now cover guard deletion in tagged
+  code, non-default dispatch, intake-data substitution, workflow/policy digest
+  mismatch, and relative/candidate-ref reusable workflow calls before candidate
+  acceptance or protected-environment access.
+
+Gate A0, iOS/TestFlight/App Store workflows, workflow implementation,
+production credentials, and a Linux-runner requirement for the macOS prototype
+remain out of scope. Human governance ratification remains independently
+tracked by `TASK-260717-2d308k`; it blocks publication, not downstream
+implementation after agent acceptance.
+
+## Artifacts and SHA-256
+
+- `docs/TASK-260715-whtdsf_ci-trust-and-quality-gate-contract.md` —
+  `6ad6fec60b12cfa2ffc7c8578ed7e27ed3c3cd6259c90675ae3303745c58f53a`
+- `diagrams/TASK-260715-whtdsf_ci-trust-boundary.puml` —
