+# TASK-260715-whtdsf — Rework 4 outcome
+
+Date: 2026-08-30 (Asia/Tbilisi)
+Base: `b3422b05226253a17676b9b84c764071fe3dbe74`
+
+## Result
+
+Ready for exact-artifact independent agent review. The CI trust and
+quality-gate contract now closes CR revision 2's release workflow-provenance
+blocker while preserving every prior accepted control.
+
+- A `v*` tag triggers only unprivileged `release-intake.yml`. Repository
+  settings enforce a read-only token, production secrets exist only in
+  protected environments restricted to the default branch, and intake exposes
+  no cache, artifact, checkout, executable output, or candidate authority.
+- Candidate acceptance occurs only in default-branch `release-prepare.yml` via
+  `workflow_run: completed`. It independently resolves run/ref/ancestry
+  metadata and rejects missing or ambiguous evidence without consuming intake
+  code, output, cache, artifact, log, or asserted verdict.
+- `github.workflow_sha`, a checked-in policy digest, and every
+  credential-capable reusable workflow's full commit SHA/file digest are bound
+  into the immutable candidate. Relative, tag, branch, candidate-ref, and
+  selectable-ref release authority is prohibited.
+- Production-call-site negative fixtures now cover guard deletion in tagged
+  code, non-default dispatch, intake-data substitution, workflow/policy digest
+  mismatch, and relative/candidate-ref reusable workflow calls before candidate
+  acceptance or protected-environment access.
+
+Gate A0, iOS/TestFlight/App Store workflows, workflow implementation,
+production credentials, and a Linux-runner requirement for the macOS prototype
+remain out of scope. Human governance ratification remains independently
+tracked by `TASK-260717-2d308k`; it blocks publication, not downstream
+implementation after agent acceptance.
+
+## Artifacts and SHA-256
+
+- `docs/TASK-260715-whtdsf_ci-trust-and-quality-gate-contract.md` —
+  `6ad6fec60b12cfa2ffc7c8578ed7e27ed3c3cd6259c90675ae3303745c58f53a`
+- `diagrams/TASK-260715-whtdsf_ci-trust-boundary.puml` —
+  `14c1556ae9b2198c74af1d5f810fba9f7364c1ed2095e9f2b622db88cdce7e7b`
+- `diagrams/artefacts/TASK-260715-whtdsf_ci-trust-boundary.svg` —
+  `175c3a64b544eef4ad8c1706b7bea007572631aaf9c123182995276284b3eda7`
+- `README.md` —
+  `5a6d83659443b8d6a5f5dfbd0fb61938b9df767267e48ddfc1637a15037adc98`
+- `LOGBOOK.md` —
+  `f8eaaa244d063b07b115416dc1c2104dd54e41a4dc592a33cdd2f2058ca8cbd5`
+
+## Validation and real exits
+
+- Required `set_status(TASK-260715-whtdsf, status=analysis)`: exit 0.
+- `task-board` readiness and scoped board query: exit 0.
+- Official GitHub workflow/trigger/reusable-workflow documentation reads: exit
+  0; findings persisted in `TASK-260715-whtdsf_github-workflow-provenance.md`.
+- Contract checker: exit 0; 27 six-field inventory rows, nine exact required
+  checks, 18 trace rows with one primary check, all required threat names, and
+  trusted-entry/provenance bounds present.
+- PlantUML readiness, `-checkonly`, SVG render, non-empty check, PNG render, and
+  manual visual inspection: exit 0.
+- Tracked and untracked whitespace checks: exit 0.
+- `task-board validate --json`: process exit 0 and content assertion exit 0;
+  `valid=true`, zero errors, zero warnings.
+- `scripts/tests/test-credential-free-validation.sh`: exit 1. It still expects
+  the deferred `ReluxProxyIOSUITests` scheme while the accepted active graph has
+  six macOS-only schemes. `Project.swift`, this test, and
+  `scripts/check-workspace-schemes.sh` are unchanged by this candidate (diff
+  exit 0). This is a pre-existing cross-owner regression, not reported as green
+  or fixed.
+- Product Swift/Go builds were not rerun because this delta changes only the
+  binding documentation, focused diagram/render, README, logbook, and board
+  outcomes; it does not change product or workflow code.
+
+## Acceptance mapping
+
+1. Contract section 3 inventories every seed, PR, intake, preparation, release,
+   and deferred workflow trigger/job with trust/input, permissions,
+   environment/secrets, network, outputs/retention, and approval.
+2. Sections 2–3 make PR/fork jobs read-only, credential-free, environment-free,
+   and non-publishing; tagged intake cannot self-elevate or reach production.
+3. Sections 4–5 bind nine checks and map all 18 requirements to exactly one
+   primary check plus macOS/iOS/relay/review ownership.
+4. Sections 7–8 cover fork, mutable action, cache, artifact, tag/workflow,
+   rerun, cancellation, concurrency, and credential threats with rejecting
+   fixtures at named production call sites.
+5. Section 9 records autonomous agent review and separately accountable human
+   ratification at `TASK-260717-2d308k`; no trust decision is silently disputed.
+
+## Board/decomposition audit and residual risk
+
+No board element or research task was created. Existing atomic owners cover all
+contract requirements; the GitHub execution-model question arose from reviewer
+evidence and was resolved from official documentation rather than becoming an
+open research task. Workflow enforcement and rejecting fixtures remain owned by
+downstream implementation tasks. Human ratification still blocks publication.
+The required `references/negative-evidence.md` remains unavailable, so its
+contents remain unknown. The pre-existing scheme-set test remains red under its
+cross-owner scope.
