Checkpoint an accepted Change Request revision.

The accepted candidate tree becomes one internal commit on the Story branch,
created under a compare-and-swap on the branch tip, and the leaf then moves to
done. Nothing is landed on trunk: internal checkpoints only delimit later Task
diffs and make the work recoverable, and the final Story squash discards them.

A Change Request with repository_delta=empty creates no commit — its tree would
equal its parent's — and the leaf still moves to done by the same mutation with
the same acknowledgement semantics.

This is the orchestrator's command. A reviewer-archetype run must not run it:
the checkpoint supplies the commit acknowledgement that closes the leaf.

